isrupts-catania-flights-again/a-79462773--6d2664a469ad.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/sicily-mount-etna-ash-disrupts-catania-flights-again/a-79462773?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A thick ash cloud from Mount Etna has been disrupting flights to Catania in Sicily for several days. Italy and Europe's most active volcano, Etna has impacted air travel several times this summer.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>SpaceX launches supersized Starship into orbit</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a0b91b44b24975d86adc1c184e40b8a502d4aad8b6ae080469c735d8fd55d6b2</id><updated>2026-09-29T05:53:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-28T15:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/spacex-launches-supersized-starship-into-orbit/a-79462696--8c10c0fa5bb3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/spacex-launches-supersized-starship-into-orbit/a-79462696?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Starship is the biggest and most powerful spacecraft ever built and it is meant to support NASA's Artemis moon program.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Turkey: Comedian convicted for 'insulting' Erdogan in show</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1ae8a6ab80100e1ee814c30434c33ffb56836128a76fec8e5520838ab72e0025</id><updated>2026-09-29T05:53:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-28T14:51:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/turkey-comedian-convicted-for-insulting-erdogan-in-show/a-79455759--b32d8c83cb81.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/turkey-comedian-convicted-for-insulting-erdogan-in-show/a-79455759?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Deniz Goktas was convicted of two of three charges, including "insulting" the president, but was released pending the appeal process. Nominally, Turkey is a secular country with free speech.</summary><category term="News